Maintainer: Mahammad Rahimov <224394699+MahammadRahimov@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), nginx, keepalived, openssl,
 curl, openssh-server, openssh-client, sqlite3, ufw, iproute2, gzip, tar, util-linux, passwd
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/MahammadRahimov/furnace
Description: Blocklist server that publishes IP and domain lists for firewalls
 Furnace keeps a blocklist of IPs and domains. A SOAR, a script or a UI adds
 and removes entries through an HTTPS API with a token. A firewall downloads
 the lists as plain text files (Palo Alto: External Dynamic Lists, EDLs) with
 a login. Two servers share one IP address with keepalived, and
 the leader copies its database to the follower every minute.
 .
 Flask and gunicorn are bundled inside the package, so it works the same on
 every supported system.
 .
 After the install, run: sudo furnace setup
